WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.920
A small plane points due north and flies
through the air at two hundred kilometres

2
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:05.960
per hour.

3
00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:10.200
But a fifty kilometre per hour
wind is blowing towards the east.

4
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.610
The nose still points north.

5
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.860
Yet the plane slides
sideways across the map.

6
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.780
So how fast is it really
going, and in which direction?

7
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.200
Do the two speeds just add
to two hundred and fifty?

8
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.500
In this mission, you'll
treat a velocity as a vector:

9
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.440
something with a size and a direction.

10
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:34.690
You'll add vectors tip to tail, and
find the size of a vector by Pythagoras.

11
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.070
Your mission: work out where
the plane actually goes,

12
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.160
and how fast.
